export default "Use this kit if you have endometriosis symptoms, a diagnosis, or are preparing for a visit or surgery.\n\nIt gives you one place for pain, bowel and bladder symptoms, diet notes, pain relief trials, imaging visits, and laparoscopy recovery.\n\nIt is a set of tracking sheets and question lists.\n\nIt is not medical advice.\n\nIt cannot diagnose endometriosis, rule it out, or replace a clinician visit.\n\nIf pain is severe, new, or unsafe to wait on, contact a clinician now.\n\n## What this kit can do\n\n| This kit can help you | This kit cannot |\n|---|---|\n| Name symptoms in plain words. | Diagnose endometriosis. |\n| Show if symptoms come near your period. | Rule out other causes. |\n| Help you prepare for a visit or surgery follow-up. | Tell you what treatment to use. |\n| Help you ask for next steps. | Replace a clinician visit. |\n\n## One-page visit packet\n\nFill out the short version first. Bring extra logs only if needed.\n\n| Topic | Your note |\n|---|---|\n| Main reason for this visit | |\n| Date symptoms started | |\n| Last 3 period start dates | |\n| Worst pain score, 0 to 10 | |\n| Where pain shows up | |\n| Bowel symptoms | |\n| Bladder symptoms | |\n| What you miss or change because of symptoms | |\n| Medicines or steps tried | |\n| Main question for the clinician | |\n\n## Symptom checklist\n\nCheck what fits. Leave the rest blank.\n\n### Pain timing\n\n- [ ] Cramps stop me from work, school, sleep, or plans.\n- [ ] Pain starts before my period.\n- [ ] Pain is worst during my period.\n- [ ] Pain happens at ovulation or between periods.\n- [ ] Pain lasts after bleeding stops.\n- [ ] Pain medicine does not help enough.\n- [ ] Pain wakes me up.\n\n### Where the pain is\n\n- [ ] Lower belly, one or both sides.\n- [ ] Lower back, hips, or thighs.\n- [ ] Rectum or anus.\n- [ ] Bladder area.\n- [ ] Deep pain inside the pelvis.\n\n### Bowel and bladder symptoms\n\n- [ ] Pain when having a bowel movement.\n- [ ] Rectal pain or pressure.\n- [ ] Constipation or diarrhea near my period.\n- [ ] Bloating or nausea near my period.\n- [ ] Pain when peeing or needing to pee more often.\n- [ ] Blood in stool or urine near my period.\n\nThese symptoms can have many causes. Write them down. Do not use them to diagnose yourself.\n\n### Sex pain, if you want to note it\n\nSkip this section if it does not apply or does not feel safe.\n\n- [ ] Deep pain during sex or pain after sex.\n- [ ] Pain is worse near my period.\n- [ ] I avoid sex because of pain.\n- [ ] I want to ask about pelvic pain in private.\n\n### Fertility questions\n\nOnly fill this out if it fits your life.\n\n| Question | Your notes |\n|---|---|\n| Are you trying to get pregnant? | |\n| How long have you been trying? | |\n| Any known fertility care or testing? | |\n| Main question for care | |\n\n## Pain map\n\nMark each place pain shows up. Add when it happens.\n\n| Pain area | During period | Before period | Ovulation time | Other days | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Lower belly or pelvis | | | | | |\n| One side of pelvis | | | | | |\n| Lower back | | | | | |\n| Rectum or deep bowel area | | | | | |\n| Bladder area | | | | | |\n| Hips, legs, or thighs | | | | | |\n\n## Daily pain log\n\nUse one row per day. Zero-pain days count too. They show when pain is absent.\n\n| Date | Cycle day | Pain location | Severity 0-10 | Duration (hrs) | What helped | What worsened | Associated symptoms |\n|---|---:|---|---:|---|---|---|---|\n| | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | |\n\nPain score guide: 0 is no pain. 5 is pain that limits but does not stop normal activity. 10 is pain requiring emergency care. Score resting pain, not pain with movement.\n\n## Bowel and bladder symptom log\n\nUse one row per day. Write what happened, not a medical word.\n\n| Date | Cycle day | Bowel movement pain 0-10 | Constipation | Diarrhea | Rectal pain or pressure | Urinary urgency | Pain when peeing | Bleeding | Notes |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| | | | none, mild, strong | none, mild, strong | none, mild, strong | none, mild, strong | none, mild, strong | stool, urine, not sure | |\n| | | | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | | | |\n\nBlood in stool or urine needs medical advice. Seek urgent care if it feels unsafe to wait. Do not assume bowel or bladder symptoms are endometriosis; infection and other causes need care too.\n\n## Diet and symptom trigger log\n\nA food log can show timing, but it cannot prove a food caused pain, bloating, bowel symptoms, or fatigue. Do not cut out whole food groups based on one bad day.\n\n| Date | Cycle day | Meals and snacks | Caffeine | Alcohol | Pain 0-10 | Bowel symptoms | Bloating | Fatigue | Notes |\n|---|---:|---|---|---|---:|---|---|---|---|\n| | | | none, some, more than usual | none, some | | none, mild, strong | none, mild, strong | none, mild, strong | |\n| | | | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | | | |\n\n## Pain relief trial log\n\nThis does not tell you what to try, give dose advice, or say when to start or stop medicine. Ask a clinician or pharmacist first.\n\n| Date | Cycle day | Time started | Pain before 0-10 | What you tried | Pain after 30 min | Pain after 1 hr | Side effects |\n|---|---:|---|---:|---|---:|---:|---|\n| | | | | heat, rest, medicine, other | | | |\n| | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | |\n\n## Laparoscopy recovery log\n\nUse this after surgery. It is not a recovery plan or timeline. Follow your surgeon's instructions and seek care for urgent or worrying symptoms.\n\n| Date | Day after surgery | Pain 0-10 | Incision notes | Bleeding notes | Bowel and bladder notes | Medicine questions | Activity and rest |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|---|---|---|\n| | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | |\n\n### Follow-up questions\n\n- What did you find during surgery? Did it confirm endometriosis?\n- Were bowel, bladder, ovary, or tube areas involved?\n- What symptoms should improve first, and what may take more time?\n- When can I return to work, school, sex, exercise, or lifting?\n- Should I keep tracking pain by cycle day, and my first period after surgery?\n\n## Ultrasound question list\n\nUse this before or after imaging. It does not read your scan or diagnose endometriosis.\n\n- What will this scan look for? Can it look for ovarian endometriomas or deep endometriosis?\n- What did the scan show, and what did it not show?\n- If my scan is normal, what does that mean? Could symptoms still fit endometriosis?\n- When would referral or laparoscopy make sense?\n- What symptoms mean I should call sooner?\n\n## Pattern review\n\nAnswer these after one cycle.\n\n| Question | Your notes |\n|---|---|\n| Which cycle days were worst? | |\n| Did symptoms start before bleeding? | |\n| Did symptoms happen outside the period? | |\n| Did bowel or bladder symptoms follow a cycle pattern? | |\n| What symptom changed daily life most? | |\n| What do you want checked first? | |\n\n## Short visit script\n\n> \"I am not trying to diagnose myself. I am using this to show a pattern. My pain or symptoms affect ________. They are worst around ________. I also notice ________. What should we check next?\"\n\nIf your visit includes sex, fertility, pregnancy, bowel, or bladder details, you can ask to speak alone.\n\n## Privacy-limited export\n\nBring the smallest useful record.\n\n| Bring | Skip unless needed |\n|---|---|\n| Last 3 to 6 period start dates | Full app export |\n| Pain score summary and pain map | Private notes not tied to care |\n| Bowel and bladder summary | Sex notes if you do not want to share them |\n| Medicines tried | Raw screenshots or old data that does not fit this visit |\n\n## Floriva note\n\nFloriva can help you keep cycle, pain, and symptom notes on your device.\n\nIt cannot diagnose endometriosis, choose treatment, or replace your care team.\n\nFor visit prep, read [Floriva for gynecologist prep](/app-guides/floriva-for-gynecologist-prep).\n</content>";
